4f8a2977566a" :question/math-academy-id "q-43768" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $R_{3}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $3$, and its subset $A$ containing all polynomials of the form $at^{3}$, where $a ∈ R$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $A$ is closed under polynomial addition\n2. $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n3. $A$ is a subspace of $R_{3}[t]$\n4. $A$ is **not** a subspace of $R_{3}[t]$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8536f8a6-1bfc-5275-95ca-8a1fda0afe28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123525} {:answer/id #uuid "b659c777-4549-54ab-9f1f-bae85db6256b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123526} {:answer/id #uuid "5da722ba-7c66-52bf-862c-fc5ad59257b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123527} {:answer/id #uuid "64f059cc-f403-5120-b592-b5803d968b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123528} {:answer/id #uuid "79c277c4-a05b-5a16-ab06-0142128ff522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123529}] :answer-field/id #uuid "856e0bc2-ed8c-5746-a814-6831d1a835e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123524}] :question/id #uuid "027d54ca-a5e1-5f8e-b0e8-aea8a3580062" :question/math-academy-id "q-43770" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $M_{2}(R)$ of all $2 \\cdot 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $C = {\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\mid a ∈ R}$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $C$ is closed under matrix addition\n2. $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n3. $C$ is a subspace of $M_{2}(R)$\n4. $C$ is **not** a subspace of $M_{2}(R)$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125155 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "809e6797-c522-5612-8bd7-cb8615d531d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123531} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c34f41-064f-5f16-aab2-eac2730d42da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123532} {:answer/id #uuid "01f80abc-829f-5786-84f6-ce1a3275419d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123533} {:answer/id #uuid "421db684-9acf-5c67-bbf1-087ecc26897f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123534} {:answer/id #uuid "7d6857c3-0a48-5ef2-9fca-96aa0ee678ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2c34f41-064f-5f16-aab2-eac2730d42da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123532} :answer-field/id #uuid "fedfc0aa-7927-5b40-97e2-4079ddb0435f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bff3a0b0-c74a-55ac-a94b-e3a390164777" :question/math-academy-id "q-43772" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$ and its subset $D$ containing all $2\\times 2$ matrices such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $1.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $D$ is closed under matrix addition\n\nII. $D$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $D$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\nIV. $D$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ are two matrices from $D$ such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $1,$ then \n\n$$\n{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}\n$$\n\n is a matrix where the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to \n\n$$\n1+1=2.\n$$\n\n This matrix does not belong to $D.$ So, $D$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $A$ is an element of $D$ such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $1,$ and $k=5\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\nkA\n$$\n\n is a matrix such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to \n\n$$\n5\\cdot 1=5.\n$$\n\n This matrix does not belong to $D.$ So, $D$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $D$ is a *not* subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1ffc5be-6eb8-5d79-a371-0f41d244eff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123543} {:answer/id #uuid "3ea96d09-2414-59e7-93d9-1c14b954d85a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123544} {:answer/id #uuid "54836036-61d0-5040-9a35-891c3ceb0772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123545} {:answer/id #uuid "5504a5b0-7336-517a-9f6f-e3a589e714ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123546} {:answer/id #uuid "652e332d-f23d-5896-af54-53390e1a7000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5504a5b0-7336-517a-9f6f-e3a589e714ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123546} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fd5febf-f795-5bf4-9d65-de01677ca83e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1b6af7e1-2428-58bf-a924-9c6a5027415f" :question/math-academy-id "q-43774" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $D=\\{f\\in C[0,1]\\,|\\,f(0)=3\\}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $D$ is closed under function addition\n\nII. $D$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $D$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n\nIV. $D$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f(x),g(x)\\in D,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(0) & =f(0)+g(0) \\\\  & =3+3 \\\\  & =6 \\\\  & \\ne 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $D$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(x)\\in D$ and $k=5\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(0) & =(5f)(0) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =15 \\\\  & \\ne 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $D$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $D$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124579 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea4038bf-34f0-58cc-a7b6-6a4c1890570f" :knowledge-point/title "The Limit at Infinity for an Unbounded Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050259 :topic/math-academy-id 1873 :topic/title "Limits at Infinity from Graphs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e61596cc-c52e-5d75-87d3-b91654188687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123597} {:answer/id #uuid "f6eddb5b-de87-5a1e